    "text": "Position 5 sits at the geographic centre of the grid, but its centrality is more than spatial. It is the only position where all four cardinal directions touch different domains. North connects to position 2 — the mind's influence descending. South connects to position 8 — the spirit's influence ascending. West connects to position 4 — the mind transitioning to body. East connects to position 6 — the body transitioning to spirit.\n\nThis creates a crossroads — the incarnation point where Mind, Body, and Spirit converge in actual lived experience. Thought must become action here. Intention must meet consequences. Spirit must inhabit flesh. Everything must pass through here. This is not optional. It is the structural law of the system.\n\nThe Shadow Patterns\n\nEvery system has its distortions. The Codex encodes these as well, and they form a pattern as precise as the positions themselves.\n\nThe Mental Bypass (1, 3, 7) — these three positions share a common shadow: they try to remain in the realm of thought and avoid embodiment. Position 1 mistakes thought for reality. Position 3 defends a narrative as if it were the self. Position 7 becomes so absorbed in self-reflection that it stops engaging with the world. All three bypass position 5 — the messy, humbling work of actual embodied experience."
